From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:18:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: Bound dependency items per firmware lane;
 runtime queue_cap/lane_cap

The firmware stalls when a dependency item sits on a lane more than 128
Works deep (native replay: max_lane_works 127 clean, 129 stall). #148
bounded that with max_queue_entries=96, the sum of unretired Works and
items over all of a queue's lanes. That is stricter than the limit, and
it throttles large submissions: on Dota (#150 timeline, T1) 89% of
submissions with 20 or more commands were deferred, their commands
reaching firmware over 2.6 ms (p50) as earlier Works retired.

Count per lane instead: each flight records the items it queued on each
of its lanes (a render's move to the fragment lane with
VDM_BARRIER_FRAGMENT), and max_lane_entries=120 bounds a lane's Works plus
items. max_lane_works=64 stays. max_queue_entries remains as an opt-in,
default 0.

Folded in:
- WIP drm/asahi: G16 bound dependency items per firmware lane
- WIP drm/asahi: G16 runtime queue_cap/lane_cap knobs, #149 cap defaults

[WIP drm/asahi: G16 runtime queue_cap/lane_cap knobs, #149 cap defaults]
Keep production's max_queue_entries=96 and make the per-lane bound
(cherry-picked from 1761082451919) opt-in with max_lane_entries=0.
debugfs asahi_m4/queue_cap and lane_cap change them at runtime for
same-session A/B; writes (and boot values) that would leave a lane
able to exceed the firmware's 128-Work dependency window are refused:
one of queue cap 1..127 or lane cap 1..127 must hold.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
